<title>RUSSIA: Russia spring grain sowing ahead of '96, beet lags.</title>
<headline>Russia spring grain sowing ahead of '96, beet lags.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's 1997 spring grain sowing campaign was 39 percent up on a year ago by April 28, with 3.65 million hectares sown against 2.63 million last year, the State Statistics Committee said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Area sown to grain did not include maize.</p>
<p>Total spring sowing was 21 percent up on year-ago levels with 4.92 million hectares sown against 4.08 million sown by the same date in 1996.</p>
<p>Sugar beet sowing had reached 180,000 hectares by April 28, 25 percent down from the same period last year.</p>
<p>The committee released the following data</p>
<p>--THOUSANDS OF HECTARES SOWN IN SPRING CAMPAIGN AS OF APRIL 28</p>
<p>				  total area	 total area</p>
<p>				 sown in 1997     sown in 1996</p>
<p>Total spring sowing	   4,918		4,081</p>
<p> grains			   3,652		2,628</p>
<p>  (of which wheat)		441		  239</p>
<p> maize				100		  176</p>
<p>  (of which for grain)	   46		   79</p>
<p> sugar beet			 180		  240</p>
<p> sunflower			  179		  269</p>
<p> vegetables			  30		   36</p>
